# apocalypse-spike.vrs: apocalypse D24, the march spike and the pathing probe (step 1, before any march code).
# March: 20 tracked CHAR_Undead_SkeletonSoldier_Armored_Farbane spawned at the pond are moved by NyarDevTools' `.devhop`
# 10 m east every 5 s, 30 times (300 m), anchored on the mark apo-s0 that moves with them, home moved too (a marching
# horde's return point moves with its front), while Chaos stands 150 m north of the line's middle, so no player is
# within 100 m of a hop. Then Chaos goes to the end point: alive, within 30 m, heights and engagement are read from the
# [DEV UNIT] lines. Pathing (design §9 D50): after a purge, 10 fresh units at the pond get their return point moved up to
# 40 m ahead toward apo-s0 (300 m east) every 5 s by `.devwalk` for 120 s, Translation untouched, so the game's own
# pathing walks them; [DEV WALK] logs arrivals (within 30 m), the farthest and the longest stall.
# Needs: NyarDevTools with .devhop .devwalk .devunits, DevChatEcho; Chaos invulnerable (true only); no purge cooldown.
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark apo-s0
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] apo-s0
chat .nyar spawn CHAR_Undead_SkeletonSoldier_Armored_Farbane 20
expect-log spawn batch: .* 0 waiting timeout=30
wait 5
chat .nyar debug here 20
expect-reply CHAR_Undead_SkeletonSoldier_Armored_Farbane
shot full apo-spike-spawn
# away: 150 m north of the middle of the line (pond x -1880 .. -1580, z -1640)
chat .devtp -1730 -1490
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 5
chat .devwhere
expect-log \[DEV WHERE\]
chat .devunits -837329073 30 apo-s0
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=20
chat .devhop -837329073 10 0 25 apo-s0 true true
expect-log \[DEV HOP\] moved=
wait 4
chat .devhop -837329073 10 0 25 apo-s0 true true
expect-log \[DEV HOP\] moved=
wait 4
chat .devhop -837329073 10 0 25 apo-s0 true true
expect-log \[DEV HOP\] moved=
wait 4
